[stderr] 
[stderr] P0 sequence is shell → prompt/answer clarity → feedback/recovery → responsive
[stderr] variants. No environment tiles, characters, portraits, item icons, effects
[stderr] library, world map, or unrelated game-art family is in scope. For every ID,
[stderr] review at 200% zoom, phone portrait, tablet, desktop, high contrast, reduced
[stderr] motion, and with images disabled; verify mapping, non-colour state, label/alt,
[stderr] safe crop, crispness, provenance/checksum, and no essential text burned into
[stderr] reusable art. Final formats, byte budgets, and store specs await target approval.
[stderr] # 04 — Audio direction
[stderr] 
[stderr] Audio is original, optional, captioned/described where it conveys state, and
[stderr] always paired with a visual/text equivalent. No chant, anthem, broadcast,
[stderr] club, or game imitation is permitted.
[stderr] 
[stderr] | ID | Cue group | Intent |
[stderr] | --- | --- | --- |
[stderr] | AUDIO-001 | Entry and round bed | Restrained, low-distraction electronic percussion with abstract crowd-energy texture; optional and volume-controlled. |
[stderr] | AUDIO-002 | Answer and streak feedback | Brief distinct correct, incorrect, and streak cues using claps and soft brass-like synth accents without sampled sports expression. |
[stderr] | AUDIO-003 | Results and completion | Warm, short celebratory sting that supports rather than replaces the readable results state. |
[stderr] 
[stderr] Final durations, quantities, loudness targets, loop policy, and generated-cue
[stderr] selection need production approval; no audio is generated by this plan.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Original-audio contract and cue IDs
[stderr] 
[stderr] Audio reinforces the original *matchday knowledge* arc: invitation, confident
[stderr] answer, rising streak, decisive result, and clear return. It shares the abstract
[stderr] broadcast-studio vocabulary of `01-creative-direction.md` and the journey map
[stderr] in `04-experience-contract.md`: bright electronic percussion, soft claps, warm
[stderr] brass-like synth accents, and abstract crowd-energy texture. It is not a real
[stderr] crowd, chant, anthem, commentary, broadcaster ident, club sound, football-game
[stderr] imitation, or vocal performance associated with a real team.
[stderr] 
[stderr] Cue IDs use `AUDIO-<FAMILY>-<NNN>` and are immutable after package reference.
[stderr] Rendered variants append `-<state>-<mix>`; a manifest records ID, source-session
[stderr] or render checksum, creator/provenance, licence, loop points, loudness/peak,
[stderr] duration, caption/description key, trigger, mix group, and review state.
[stderr] Essential state also has text, icon/pattern, and semantic announcement. Captions
[stderr] describe function (for example, “brief rising streak cue”); missing audio never
[stderr] blocks an action.
[stderr] 
[stderr] P0 is instrumental only: no intelligible vocals, sampled speech, commentary,
[stderr] chants, crowd recordings, or copyrighted musical imitation. Original/properly
[stderr] licensed sources only; generated cues retain settings and receive human
[stderr] originality review.
[stderr] 
[stderr] | Stable ID | Purpose, journey, and trigger | Target loop / duration | Acceptance and accessibility |
[stderr] | --- | --- | --- | --- |
[stderr] | `AUDIO-MUS-001` | Home/round-choice invitation bed; J0/J2 after screen settles. | Seamless 20–40 s loop with clean entry/exit. | Low-distraction music; mute/fade immediately; never masks UI feedback or speech. |
[stderr] | `AUDIO-QZ-001` | Prompt-ready tick; J1/J2 when an unresolved card is actionable. | One-shot ≤0.5 s. | Caption “Question ready”; visible/announced card is complete without it. |
[stderr] | `AUDIO-QZ-002` | Correct confirmation; J1/J2 after adjudication. | One-shot ≤0.8 s. | Caption “Correct cue”; distinguishable from incorrect without pitch alone; never precedes written result. |
[stderr] | `AUDIO-QZ-003` | Incorrect correction; J1/J2 after adjudication. | One-shot ≤0.8 s. | Caption “Answer correction cue”; calm/non-punitive; explanation remains primary. |
[stderr] | `AUDIO-QZ-004` | Streak threshold rise; J1/J2 on confirmed 3+ streak. | One-shot ≤1.2 s. | Caption “Streak rises”; one per card; suppressible under reduced feedback. |
[stderr] | `AUDIO-RES-001` | Results sting; J1/J2 when results first appear. | One-shot 2–4 s, never loops. | Caption “Round complete”; controls available immediately and meaningful muted. |
[stderr] | `AUDIO-SET-001` | Player-requested settings preview; J0 after audio preference change. | One-shot ≤0.5 s. | Obeys current volume/mute; visible labelled test control; never autoplays on Settings open. |
[stderr] | `AUDIO-SYS-001` | Package update ready/applied; J5 at a between-round state only. | One-shot ≤0.7 s. | Caption “Update ready/applied”; visible keyboard-accessible status/action. |
[stderr] | `AUDIO-SYS-002` | Save/recovery attention; J3 when recovery panel appears. | One-shot ≤0.7 s. | Caption “Save attention cue”; non-alarming, non-looping, never replaces recovery choices. |
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Playback and mixing policy
[stderr] 
[stderr] Provide persistent per-local-profile master mute and independent music/feedback
[stderr] controls. Honour platform/system volume, audio focus/interruption, and exposed
[stderr] reduced-sensory preferences. Backgrounding pauses nonessential playback and
[stderr] never affects game state. Do not autoplay audible music before player
[stderr] interaction where platform policy requires it.
[stderr] 
[stderr] The same IDs serve responsive web, PWA, Android, and iPhone. Web/PWA waits for
[stderr] audio unlock and silently retains captions/text if unavailable; phones respect
[stderr] mute switch/audio focus. Keyboard, touch, mouse, and gamepad invoke the same
[stderr] semantic state and therefore the same cue. Remote/TV delivery is out of P0.
[stderr] 
[stderr] Production tests cover speakers/headphones, system muted, audio unavailable,
[stderr] screen-reader speech, interruption, offline cached assets, and reduced feedback.
[stderr] Acceptance requires intended trigger once at safe state, correct loop/duration,
[stderr] no required audio-only meaning, caption key, mute/volume support, permitted
[stderr] source, and complete manifest provenance/checksum/review. Exact final rendered
[stderr] count, loudness readings, formats, size budget, and language captions await
[stderr] production approval; this plan creates or licenses no audio.
