s\nproduced.\n\nWriting is precise, lively, inclusive, and fact-first: short prompts,\nunambiguous instructions, plain-language adjudication, and celebratory but\nnon-taunting feedback. Authors avoid stereotypes, unreviewed claims, and\nimitation of reference publications.\n\n## Visual and audio intent\n\nVisual direction: original modern football-broadcast graphics, bold accessible\ncategory colours, large score numerals, readable typography, disciplined card\ngeometry, clear answer states, and restrained motion. Prompt hierarchy comes\nfirst, answer action second, score/streak third. Colour is never the only cue;\nthe system supports adjustable text, focus, reduced motion, high contrast,\ncaptions, and responsive portrait-first layouts. Use original abstract pitch\nlines, stat blocks, signal sweeps, and celebration shapes\u2014never real club,\ncompetition, broadcaster, publisher, or QuizUp marks, kit designs, screenshots,\nor screen composition.\n\nAudio direction: an original restrained percussive entry bed; distinct correct,\nincorrect, streak, optional urgency, and completion cues; and a warm short\nresults sting. Bright electronic percussion, claps, soft brass-like synth\naccents, and abstract crowd energy are allowed; sampled or imitated chants,\nanthems, broadcasts, clubs, or games are not. Essential meaning always has\ntext/visual alternatives plus volume, mute, and caption/description options.\nExact cue quantities/durations/loop policy remain production decisions.\n\nThe Athletic and QuizUp are functional references only: no copying of branding,\nquestions, wording, copy, art, audio, layouts, flow choreography, or distinctive\ninteractions. All expression is independently authored.\n# 04 \u2014 Asset direction\n\nAll asset groups use the original abstract broadcast-studio direction established\nin `01-creative-direction.md`; they must not reproduce clubs, competitions,\nbroadcasters, The Athletic, QuizUp, kit designs, screenshots, or layouts.\n\n| ID | Asset group | Direction and accessibility boundary |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| ASSET-001 | Category and round graphics | Original bold category fields, abstract pitch lines, stat blocks, and signal sweeps; labels and shapes carry meaning beyond colour. |\n| ASSET-002 | Answer and score feedback | Original correct/incorrect/streak/completion state motifs with text, icon, and motion-reduced alternatives. |\n| ASSET-003 | Install and responsive shell art | Original neutral app-mark and scalable studio surfaces; no real team, competition, or reference-product marks. |\n\nAsset quantities, file formats, and final delivery budgets remain pending target\nand packaging decisions. Each asset requires provenance and human creative\nreview before production use.\n\n## Original-asset contract\n\nThe asset language is the same original *matchday knowledge* studio described\nin `01-creative-direction.md` and `04-experience-contract.md`: category fields,\npitch-line geometry, stat blocks, signal sweeps, and celebration shapes. It\nmust not become a stadium, club, competition, broadcaster, player, kit, crest,\nor reference-product trade dress. This non-fiction trivia release has no\nfictional characters, locations, dialogue portraits, maps, or gameplay worlds.\n\nIDs use `ASSET-<FAMILY>-<NNN>` and are immutable once a package references\nthem. Variants append `-<state>-<size>` (for example,\n`ASSET-FBK-001-correct-2x`); locale is a manifest field, not baked into a\nuniversal visual. The asset manifest records ID, version, source/checksum,\nowner, licence/provenance, alt-text/meaning, variants, and review status.\n\nEvery release asset is created for this project or has documented rights. Do\nnot trace, scrape, prompt for, or modify a reference screenshot, mark, kit,\nphoto, or distinctive layout. Generated output retains prompt/model/version\nand gets human originality review; third-party material needs licence and\nattribution review. Uncertain provenance, embedded unlocalisable essential\ntext, missing alt/meaning treatment, or failed contrast/state review rejects\nthe asset. Decorative absence may fall back gracefully; required UI/state\nassets reject a release.\n\n## Families, variants, and acceptance\n\n| Stable ID / priority | Purpose and screens | Required variants | Accessibility / acceptance |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `ASSET-SHL-001` / P0 | App mark and quiet studio background: Home, install, results. | light/dark/high-contrast; phone/tablet/desktop crops; static. | Mark has an accessible name; background is decorative and preserves text/control contrast and safe areas. |\n| `ASSET-QZ-001` / P0 | Reusable prompt-card field: First Whistle and standard question. | four category tokens; narrow/wide; no-text base. | Texture has no semantic meaning; prompt remains live scalable text. |\n| `ASSET-QZ-002` / P0 | Category/round tile: choice and unavailable theme. | world/domestic/club/records; available/unavailable/selected/focus. | Label plus pattern distinguishes category; unavailable has explicit text and 3:1 boundaries. |\n| `ASSET-UI-001` / P0 | Icons for pause, settings, resume, back, audio, captions, install. | default/focus/disabled/high-contrast; vector/1x/2x. | Icons supplement labels or have exact accessible names; non-colour focus and 44 \u00d7 44 CSS px target. |\n| `ASSET-UI-003` / P0 | Pause, confirmation, recovery-panel framing. | normal/high-contrast/reduced-motion; modal/non-modal. | No essential text baked in; frame cannot cover focused action. |\n| `ASSET-FBK-001` / P0 | Correct motif: rising signal/check and score increment. | correct/static/reduced-motion/high-contrast. | Written \u201cCorrect\u201d, answer, and icon/pattern remain if art/motion/audio is absent. |\n| `ASSET-FBK-002` / P0 | Incorrect motif: calm correction marker/explanation lead-in. | incorrect/static/reduced-motion/high-contrast. | Never punitive; written outcome/explanation are primary. |\n| `ASSET-FBK-003` / P0 | Streak stat block/celebration shape. | streak-3/streak-4-plus/static/reduced-motion. | Score/streak is text; no flash above three per second. |\n| `ASSET-FBK-004` / P0 | Completion/result celebration shape. | complete/replay/static/reduced-motion/high-contrast. | Results remain understandable without it; it cannot cover actions. |\n| `ASSET-SYS-001` / P0 | Offline, update, cached-package, and error symbols. | ready/offline/downloading/failed/recovery. | Icon, text, and pattern pair; semantic UI announces errors. |\n| `ASSET-OPS-001` / P1 | Internal editorial provenance/validation glyphs; J4 only. | draft/reviewed/blocked/published/withdrawn. | Text status is mandatory; icons cannot grant publication eligibility. |\n| `ASSET-MKT-001` / P1 | Store/PWA listing imagery from studio system. | platform ratios; accessible preview copy; no-text master. | Shows actual capabilities, original art, approved alt copy; not needed to play. |\n\nP0 sequence is shell \u2192 prompt/answer clarity \u2192 feedback/recovery \u2192 responsive\nvariants. No environment tiles, characters, portraits, item icons, effects\nlibrary, world map, or unrelated game-art family is in scope. For every ID,\nreview at 200% zoom, phone portrait, tablet, desktop, high contrast, reduced\nmotion, and with images disabled; verify mapping, non-colour state, label/alt,\nsafe crop, crispness, provenance/checksum, and no essential text burned into\nreusable art. Final formats, byte budgets, and store specs await target approval.\n# 04 \u2014 Audio direction\n\nAudio is original, optional, captioned/described where it conveys state, and\nalways paired with a visual/text equivalent. No chant, anthem, broadcast,\nclub, or game imitation is permitted.\n\n| ID | Cue group | Intent |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| AUDIO-001 | Entry and round bed | Restrained, low-distraction electronic percussion with abstract crowd-energy texture; optional and volume-controlled. |\n| AUDIO-002 | Answer and streak feedback | Brief distinct correct, incorrect, and streak cues using claps and soft brass-like synth accents without sampled sports expression. |\n| AUDIO-003 | Results and completion | Warm, short celebratory sting that supports rather than replaces the readable results state. |\n\nFinal durations, quantities, loudness targets, loop policy, and generated-cue\nselection need production approval; no audio is generated by this plan.\n\n## Original-audio contract and cue IDs\n\nAudio reinforces the original *matchday knowledge* arc: invitation, confident\nanswer, rising streak, decisive result, and clear return. It shares the abstract\nbroadcast-studio vocabulary of `01-creative-direction.md` and the journey map\nin `04-experience-contract.md`: bright electronic percussion, soft claps, warm\nbrass-like synth accents, and abstract crowd-energy texture. It is not a real\ncrowd, chant, anthem, commentary, broadcaster ident, club sound, football-game\nimitation, or vocal performance associated with a real team.\n\nCue IDs use `AUDIO-<FAMILY>-<NNN>` and are immutable after package reference.\nRendered variants append `-<state>-<mix>`; a manifest records ID, source-session\nor render checksum, creator/provenance, licence, loop points, loudness/peak,\nduration, caption/description key, trigger, mix group, and review state.\nEssential state also has text, icon/pattern, and semantic announcement. Captions\ndescribe function (for example, \u201cbrief rising streak cue\u201d); missing audio never\nblocks an action.\n\nP0 is instrumental only: no intelligible vocals, sampled speech, commentary,\nchants, crowd recordings, or copyrighted musical imitation. Original/properly\nlicensed sources only; generated cues retain settings and receive human\noriginality review.\n\n| Stable ID | Purpose, journey, and trigger | Target loop / duration | Acceptance and accessibility |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `AUDIO-MUS-001` | Home/round-choice invitation bed; J0/J2 after screen settles. | Seamless 20\u201340 s loop with clean entry/exit. | Low-distraction music; mute/fade immediately; never masks UI feedback or speech. |\n| `AUDIO-QZ-001` | Prompt-ready tick; J1/J2 when an unresolved card is actionable. | One-shot \u22640.5 s. | Caption \u201cQuestion ready\u201d; visible/announced card is complete without it. |\n| `AUDIO-QZ-002` | Correct confirmation; J1/J2 after adjudication. | One-shot \u22640.8 s. | Caption \u201cCorrect cue\u201d; distinguishable from incorrect without pitch alone; never precedes written result. |\n| `AUDIO-QZ-003` | Incorrect correction; J1/J2 after adjudication. | One-shot \u22640.8 s. | Caption \u201cAnswer correction cue\u201d; calm/non-punitive; explanation remains primary. |\n| `AUDIO-QZ-004` | Streak threshold rise; J1/J2 on confirmed 3+ streak. | One-shot \u22641.2 s. | Caption \u201cStreak rises\u201d; one per card; suppressible under reduced feedback. |\n| `AUDIO-RES-001` | Results sting; J1/J2 when results first appear. | One-shot 2\u20134 s, never loops. | Caption \u201cRound complete\u201d; controls available immediately and meaningful muted. |\n| `AUDIO-SET-001` | Player-requested settings preview; J0 after audio preference change. | One-shot \u22640.5 s. | Obeys current volume/mute; visible labelled test control; never autoplays on Settings open. |\n| `AUDIO-SYS-001` | Package update ready/applied; J5 at a between-round state only. | One-shot \u22640.7 s. | Caption \u201cUpdate ready/applied\u201d; visible keyboard-accessible status/action. |\n| `AUDIO-SYS-002` | Save/recovery attention; J3 when recovery panel appears. | One-shot \u22640.7 s. | Caption \u201cSave attention cue\u201d; non-alarming, non-looping, never replaces recovery choices. |\n\n## Playback and mixing policy\n\nProvide persistent per-local-profile master mute and independent music/feedback\ncontrols. Honour platform/system volume, audio focus/interruption, and exposed\nreduced-sensory preferences. Backgrounding pauses nonessential playback and\nnever affects game state. Do not autoplay audible music before player\ninteraction where platform policy requires it.\n\nThe same IDs serve responsive web, PWA, Android, and iPhone. Web/PWA waits for\naudio unlock and silently retains captions/text if unavailable; phones respect\nmute switch/audio focus. Keyboard, touch, mouse, and gamepad invoke the same\nsemantic state and therefore the same cue. Remote/TV delivery is out of P0.\n\nProduction tests cover speakers/headphones, system muted, audio unavailable,\nscreen-reader speech, interruption, offline cached assets, and reduced feedback.\nAcceptance requires intended trigger once at safe state, correct loop/duration,\nno required audio-only meaning, caption key, mute/volume support, permitted\nsource, and complete manifest provenance/checksum/review. Exact final rendered\ncount, loudness readings, formats, size budget, and language captions await\nproduction approval; this plan creates or licenses no audio.\n16-\n17-\n18-ID_PATTERNS = {\n19-    \"game\": re.compile(r\"\\bGAME-[A-Z0-9-]+\\b\"),\n20:    \"assets\": re.compile(r\"\\bASSET-[A-Z0-9-]+\\b\"),\n21:    \"audio\": re.compile(r\"\\bAUDIO-[A-Z0-9-]+\\b\"),\n22-    \"narrative\": re.compile(r\"\\bNAR-[A-Z0-9-]+\\b\"),\n23-}\n24-\n25-\n--\n124-        errors.append(\"creative_coverage must be an object\")\n125-        coverage = {}\n126-    expected = {\n127-        \"game\": identifiers(specification / \"02-game-design-bible.md\", \"game\"),\n128:        \"assets\": identifiers(specification / \"04-asset-direction.md\", \"assets\"),\n129:        \"audio\": identifiers(specification / \"04-audio-direction.md\", \"audio\"),\n130-        \"narrative\": identifiers(specification / \"02-narrative-content-model.md\", \"narrative\"),\n131-    }\n132-    selected_modules: set[str] = set()\n133-    design_units: list[dict[str, object]] = []\n--\n152-        if not design_units:\n153-            errors.append(\"game design bible needs non-empty design_units\")\n154-        if not expected[\"game\"]:\n155-            errors.append(\"