ared, narrative 0 declared. PASS: every declared creative item has an owned implementation route.\",\"browser_log\":\"\",\"screenshots\":[]},\"acceptance_results\":[{\"criterion\":\"Navigation, empty/error states, feedback, destructive actions, and privacy-sensitive content are specified.\",\"status\":\"pass\",\"evidence\":\"04-experience-contract.md specifies IA routes, unavailable/empty/error/recovery states, feedback, confirmations for abandon/reset/delete, and diagnostics consent/data boundaries.\"},{\"criterion\":\"Tokens, keyboard behaviour, focus, screen-reader labels, contrast, touch targets, and reduced motion are defined.\",\"status\":\"pass\",\"evidence\":\"04-experience-contract.md defines FT tokens, keyboard/gamepad interactions, focus placement, semantic labels/live regions, contrast thresholds, 44 \u00d7 44 targets, and reduced-motion replacements.\"},{\"criterion\":\"The proposed experience is original and does not reproduce a reference product's trade dress.\",\"status\":\"pass\",\"evidence\":\"01-creative-direction.md and 04-experience-contract.md limit references to capability outcomes and prohibit copied marks, wording, layout, choreography, art, and audio.\"},{\"criterion\":\"Where visual assets are in scope, the asset plan assigns stable, product-specific asset-family IDs, purpose, variants, provenance/originality, accessibility, and acceptance requirements.\",\"status\":\"pass\",\"evidence\":\"04-asset-direction.md declares 12 stable ASSET family IDs with purpose, states, provenance, accessibility, and acceptance requirements; each now has implementation coverage.\"},{\"criterion\":\"Where audio is in scope, the cue map assigns stable, product-specific cue IDs and purpose, loop/duration, interaction trigger, and acceptance requirements.\",\"status\":\"pass\",\"evidence\":\"04-audio-direction.md declares nine stable AUDIO cue IDs with journey/trigger, duration or loop target, mixing/accessibility, and acceptance requirements; each now has implementation coverage.\"},{\"criterion\":\"For every game and narrative-led product, creative, narrative, visual, and audio documents share a traceable premise/tone/content vocabulary and map their first-release locations, characters, scenes, UI states, and cues to user/player journeys.\",\"status\":\"pass\",\"evidence\":\"The non-fiction game deliberately has no narrative module; 01-creative-direction.md, 04-experience-contract.md, 04-asset-direction.md, and 04-audio-direction.md share the matchday-knowledge abstract-studio vocabulary and map J0\u2013J5 to screens, assets, and cues.\"}],\"documentation\":{\"reviewed_files\":[\"projects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/01-creative-direction.md\",\"projects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md\",\"projects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/04-experience-contract.md\",\"projects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/04-asset-direction.md\",\"projects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/04-audio-direction.md\",\"projects/football-trivia-e2e/planning/implementation-catalogue-index.json\"],\"updated_files\":[\"projects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/04-asset-direction.md\",\"projects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/04-audio-direction.md\",\"projects/football-trivia-e2e/planning/implementation-catalogue-index.json\"],\"summary\":\"Removed obsolete generic creative IDs from direction documents and aligned the implementation catalogue\u2019s ownership/coverage entries to the stable detailed asset and audio IDs.\"},\"known_limitations\":[],\"browser_coverage\":\"Not applicable: specification and planning-catalogue-only change; no runtime/browser behaviour changed.\",\"recommended_next_step\":\"complete\"}\ndiff --git a/projects/football-trivia-e2e/planning/implementation-catalogue-index.json b/projects/football-trivia-e2e/planning/implementation-catalogue-index.json\nindex c729989c4ea231de5af911082b6239ee08840288..0666616155643de6e452550fb1473a3d3fdabce8\n--- a/projects/football-trivia-e2e/planning/implemen